{%- comment -%}
  templates/page.my-athoor-wishlist.liquid — the Your wishlist page (spec task 19.4).

  Requirements 15.1, 16.1, 6.3.

  N4/N5. The account is the single source of truth; the device list is reconciled into it.

  ── BRANCH B (D1 / OQ-1) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  The store uses Shopify's NEW customer accounts: `/account` redirects to
  `shopify.com/<id>/account`, so it is Shopify-hosted and `templates/customers/*`
  are dead files for the portal. §17.2's Branch B therefore puts every portal
  destination on its own Shopify page, and this is one of them. Nothing under
  `templates/customers/` is read or modified by the portal.

  ── WHY THIS FILE IS FOUR LINES OF LOGIC ──────────────────────────────────────
  Every gate, every landmark and every asset tag lives in `portal-chrome`, which is
  rendered once here. Ten templates that each evaluated the feature flag would be
  ten chances for one of them to evaluate it differently — and §25.2 requires the
  flag to be read in one server-side place before any portal markup exists.

  With the flag off this renders `page.content` and nothing else: no portal markup,
  no stylesheet, no script. That is what makes the flag-off response byte-identical
  to a plain Shopify page (Requirement 22.2).
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- capture portal_section -%}{% render 'portal-section', name: 'wishlist' %}{%- endcapture -%}
{% render 'portal-chrome',
  section_name: 'wishlist',
  nav_key: 'wishlist',
  page_title: 'Your wishlist',
  content: portal_section
%}
